<title>THAILAND: Asset Plus sees gains on Thai Eastern Water IPO.</title>
<headline>Asset Plus sees gains on Thai Eastern Water IPO.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern Water Plc shares should rise between 12-40 percent over a projected initial offer price of 25 baht per share when the stock debuts on the Thai bourse next month, Asset Plus Securities said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Assuming an IPO (initial public offer) price of 25 baht, the upside potential is between 12 percent to 40 percent,&quot; the firm said in a report.</p>
<p>Asset Plus said the virtual monopoly position Eastern Water enjoys in supplying some of Thailand's most heavily industrialised areas on the eastern seaboard makes the stock an attractive prospect for investors.</p>
</text>
